WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.656 --> 00:00:14.496
It's an open secret in the industry: shops tied to wedding planners are forced into a volume-driven model because of low per-client rates and commission cuts.

2
00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:27.504
Only part of what the customer pays reaches the shop, so it's compensated with a high volume of clients, and the wedding-parent makeup often ends up in the hands of weekend part-timers or junior staff.

3
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:35.952
By contrast, a shop you research and book yourself is more likely to give you high-quality, dedicated service that matches what you're paying.

4
00:00:36.288 --> 00:00:47.736
It also lets you pick a genuinely skilled artist suited to your parents' face shape and hair concerns, rather than the planner's preference — leading to much higher satisfaction.

5
00:00:48.072 --> 00:00:53.448
I'd recommend finding your own shop rather than going with your wedding planner's recommendation.
